        <mxCell id="zFlow" value="FLOWS AND DESIGN NOTES" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F7FAFD;strokeColor=#1F5B96;strokeWidth=1.5;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F5B96;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="360" width="1420" height="255" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f0" value="1  CORRECTED: westus2 peers to BOTH centralus and eastus2 - the original design peered to eastus2 only, which had no working identity path during an eastus2 outage" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B77300;fontSize=11;fontColor=#B77300;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="400" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f1" value="2  DR session host DNS order: centralus DC first (10.20.1.4), eastus2 DC second - centralus survives an eastus2 failure, so it is the primary path, not a fallback" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="440" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f2" value="3  westus2's subnet (10.30.0.0/16) is mapped to centralus-Site in AD Sites and Services - no dedicated westus2 domain controller needed" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="480" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3" value="4  During an eastus2 outage: DR session hosts authenticate via centralus only - the failed region is never in the authentication path" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="520" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f4" value="5  Capacity reservation is OFF by default (enable_capacity_reservation=false) - bills continuously at full VM rate when enabled, confirmed against Microsoft's own documentation" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B77300;fontSize=11;fontColor=#B77300;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="560" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f5" value="6  No new workspace: a failed-over user's desktop entry is the SAME one they always had, now pointing at westus2 infrastructure" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="600" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="foot" value="Original architecture diagram created for this book. Not a Microsoft diagram. Corrected pass: identity dependency on failed region removed. Verified against terraform/lab19-dr-failover, August 2026. Self-contained shapes, no remote icon dependency." style="text;fontSize=10;fontColor=#605E5C;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="635" width="1300" height="20" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
